// repoHooksDirCache memoizes the hooks directory per explicit repository root.
//
// The hook hot path resolves this repeatedly: turn start runs the integration
// coordinator, which asks for the hooks dir once per inspection, once per
// snapshot, and once more to verify — each one a `git rev-parse --git-path
// hooks` fork at ~10ms. Within a single process the answer cannot change, so
// the fork is pure waste; GetHooksDir next door has memoized its cwd-relative
// twin for exactly this reason since long before the integration coordinator
// existed.
//
// Keyed by resolved absolute root rather than by cwd, so a caller acting on a
// repo passed as an argument gets the answer for that repo and not for
// whichever one the process happens to be running in.
//
// Deliberately NOT folded into getHooksDirInPath: that primitive stays
// uncached because TestGetHooksDirInPath_CoreHooksPath rewrites
// core.hooksPath between two calls for the same directory and requires the
// second answer to reflect the change. Callers wanting a fresh read keep
// using the primitive; callers on the hot path use this.
